// Slow report: the calculated columns and measures slow reports usually carry.
// Every measure returns the same numbers as the fixed report (../06-checks.md); only the speed and size differ.
// Same names and format strings as ../03-measures.dax. No display folders: the measures sit loose on Sales.
//
// Measures by page:
//   Overview cards:      Sales Amount, Sales YoY %, Margin %, Orders, Avg Order Value, Customers
//   Overview charts:     Sales Amount, Sales PY
//   Products table:      Sales Amount, Sales PY, Sales YoY %, Margin %, Customers, Product Rank
//   Products matrix:     Sales Amount, Sales YoY %, Margin %
//   Helpers (no visual): Total Cost, Margin

// ===== Calculated columns on Sales (Table tools > New column); types and formats in 02-model.md =====

Line Amount = Sales[Quantity] * Sales[Net Price]

Line Cost = Sales[Quantity] * Sales[Unit Cost]

Line Margin = Sales[Line Amount] - Sales[Line Cost]

Year = YEAR ( Sales[Order Date] )

Month = FORMAT ( Sales[Order Date], "mmm" )

Month Number = MONTH ( Sales[Order Date] )


// ===== Measures on Sales (Table tools > New measure) =====

// Sales Amount: revenue in US dollars, summed from the stored Line Amount column.
// Format: \$#,0
Sales Amount =
SUMX ( Sales, Sales[Line Amount] )

// Total Cost: cost in US dollars, summed from the stored Line Cost column.
// Format: \$#,0
Total Cost =
SUMX ( Sales, Sales[Line Cost] )

// Margin: summed from the stored Line Margin column.
// Format: \$#,0
Margin =
SUMX ( Sales, Sales[Line Margin] )

// Margin %: Margin as a share of Sales Amount.
// Slow: the same measure is evaluated again and again instead of once into a variable.
// Format: 0.0%
Margin % =
IF ( [Sales Amount] = 0, BLANK (), [Margin] / [Sales Amount] )

// Orders: number of distinct orders.
// Slow: a whole table of order keys is built just to count it.
// Format: #,0
Orders =
COUNTROWS ( SUMMARIZE ( Sales, Sales[Order Key] ) )

// Customers: number of distinct customers who bought.
// Slow: same pattern as Orders.
// Format: #,0
Customers =
COUNTROWS ( SUMMARIZE ( Sales, Sales[Customer Key] ) )

// Avg Order Value: Sales Amount per order.
// Slow: iterates every order and recalculates Sales Amount for each one (context transition).
// Format: \$#,0.00
Avg Order Value =
AVERAGEX ( VALUES ( Sales[Order Key] ), [Sales Amount] )

// Sales PY: Sales Amount for the same months one year earlier.
// Written by hand on the Year column, because there is no date table.
// Format: \$#,0
Sales PY =
CALCULATE (
    [Sales Amount],
    FILTER ( ALL ( Sales[Year] ), Sales[Year] = MAX ( Sales[Year] ) - 1 )
)

// Sales YoY %: change against the previous year; blank when there is no previous year.
// Slow: Sales PY is evaluated up to three times.
// Format: 0.0%
Sales YoY % =
IF ( [Sales PY] = 0, BLANK (), ( [Sales Amount] - [Sales PY] ) / [Sales PY] )

// Product Rank: the product's place by Sales Amount among the products in the current filters.
// Format: 0
Product Rank =
IF ( ISBLANK ( [Sales Amount] ), BLANK (), RANKX ( ALL ( Sales[Product Name] ), [Sales Amount] ) )
